Looking at this problem, I need to find the maximum number of subsets of a 10-element set such that any two distinct subsets are either disjoint or one properly contains the other. This is exactly a **laminar family**.

**Answer Leak Check:** The problem statement contains no leaked answers or solution hints. Proceeding to solve.

